WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:01.800
President Reif:
Online learning has

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.880
become an indispensable
tool, not just for university

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.520
students and professionals, but
for anyone who wants to learn.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.750
Over the past decade, the
immensely talented MITx team

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.200
has helped shape
that experience.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.700
Sanjay Sarma: Our
education is going

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.070
through an extraordinary
transformation right now,

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:30.100
and MIT is making a statement
to the world through MITx.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.833
And MIT is also transforming
itself through MITx.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.750
Eric Grimson: The fact
that you can get access

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.920
to MIT-quality courses if you've
got internet connection is just

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.360
an incredible impact.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.910
Ana Bell: The only thing that
matters is a desire to learn,

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.140
and it's never
too late to start.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.740
Krishna Rajagopal: It's
an extraordinary learning

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.490
opportunity for millions
of independent learners

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.425
openly available to anyone,
anywhere, anytime, any place.

00:00:58.232 --> 00:01:00.690
Eric Grimson: There are more
learners around the world that

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.700
have completed
successfully a course

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.150
than we have living MIT alumni.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:11.700
That's broadening our reach in
a way that just is striking.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.970
Aditya Joshi: Online
learning opens up

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:19.050
the opportunity to engage
with people around the world.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.260
Meghan Perdue: All these people
can come to the same course

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.440
with different goals, interests,
and levels of engagement

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.150
and find what
they're looking for.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.412
And that's pretty magical.

00:01:29.412 --> 00:01:31.120
Sanjay Sarma: On MITx
you can experiment.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.530
You can put in simulations, you
can put in a game, a drawing

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.770
program, and it has
helped the world

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.480
recognize the value of online.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.450
It's great that MIT
took a lead 10 years ago

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.810
to make this happen.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.810
Mary Ellen Wiltrout: We
didn't know 10 years ago

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.000
that understanding what
MRNA is would become

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
a common conversation, but
our courses can help people

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.880
with that understanding.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.760
From deciding a major in
a specific discipline,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.970
to applying to a new job,
to truly living the concept

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.950
of lifelong learning
during retirement.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.320
You invest in yourself
by learning something

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.500
you could not have otherwise,
and a success could literally

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.820
change your life.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.970
10 years of MITx is a testament
to how important education

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.650
is at any level.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.340
Krishna Rajagopal: We're in the
10th year of MITx version one,

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.160
but just at the very beginning
of the MITx for the future.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.877
And that's what makes things
so exciting at this moment.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.710
Eric Grimson: I've been
stopped in airports,

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.280
in hotel lobbies by people
who say, I took your course

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.310
and it changed my career path.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.070
It's not just me, but
that's other people

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.240
offering MIT courses.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.050
You're changing people's lives
in a really positive way.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.350
That's both the excitement
and the spirit of MITx.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.500
President Reif MITx,
congratulations

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.160
and happy anniversary.

